{"lines":[{"w":0.016427103678385416,"h":0.013081394746943587,"x":0.084188912123846313,"c":1,"y":0.093023256005888677,"t":"D"},{"c":1,"h":0.014534883302221524,"x":0.080082135213695005,"t":"G","y":0.67587209308726137,"w":0.018480493227640796},{"c":1,"w":0.083057225545247415,"y":0.047087508129895927,"h":0.015747165961251475,"t":"Reading","x":0.83529207245478521},{"c":1,"x":0.11490805109782438,"y":0.092093841826320966,"t":"The first known record of a named group of Mediterranean pirates, made during the rule of","w":0.78454640706380208,"h":0.019693655953646361},{"c":1,"w":0.78028747558593736,"t":"ancient Egyptian Pharaoh Akhenaten (c 1353-1336 BCE), was in the Amarna Letters. These","x":0.1293634482964191,"y":0.11032448392735639,"h":0.017699115044247815},{"w":0.77618067423502601,"c":1,"t":"were extracts of diplomatic correspondence between the pharaoh and his allies, and covered","x":0.12936346154444589,"y":0.12936046523079114,"h":0.016067263510374907},{"t":"many pressing issues, including piracy. It seems the pharaoh was troubled by two distinct","y":0.14680232568284257,"h":0.016029532891107423,"x":0.12936344770374092,"w":0.75564682006835948,"c":1},{"h":0.019189747948210489,"t":"pirate groups, the Lukka and the Sherden. Despite the Egyptian fleet's best efforts, the pirates","x":0.12930369715406906,"c":1,"y":0.16418723547629943,"w":0.78656636555989579},{"w":0.75384048461914055,"x":0.12720397460631225,"h":0.021778433020487653,"t":"continued to cause substantial disruption to regional commerce. In the letters, the king of","y":0.17941403732247807,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.20058139546286335,"h":0.015988371857499684,"t":"Alashiya (modern Cyprus) rejected Akhenaten's claims of a connection with the Lukka","x":0.12936346017414924,"w":0.73511291503906251},{"h":0.015996089586466145,"c":1,"y":0.2194690265725836,"w":0.76796712239583331,"x":0.12731007319111332,"t":"(based in modern-day Turkey). The king assured Akhenaten he was prepared to punish any"},{"w":0.28747433980305992,"x":0.12731005790927014,"t":"of his subjects involved in piracy.","c":1,"h":0.016033820205733518,"y":0.23687315641367834},{"y":0.26453488383628421,"t":"The ancient Greek world's experience of piracy was different from that of Egyptian rulers.","x":0.12731006676116902,"w":0.7659137471516928,"h":0.015996089586466145,"c":1},{"y":0.27998083730332191,"t":"While Egypt's power was land-based, the ancient Greeks relied on the Mediterranean in","x":0.1292403493167269,"w":0.7415189615885418,"h":0.021472433534695301,"c":1},{"w":0.73730275472005224,"y":0.2987999065906024,"h":0.019531440172223524,"x":0.12725248283546867,"c":1,"t":"almost all aspects of life, from trade to warfare. Interestingly, in his works the Iliad and"},{"y":0.31669846976801463,"t":"the Odyssey, the ancient Greek writer Homer not only condones, but praises the lifestyle","w":0.74755966186523448,"x":0.12724372591764449,"h":0.019128780308726334,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.12731005314492005,"w":0.73716634114583324,"y":0.33569321533688878,"t":"and actions of pirates. The opinion remained unchanged in the following centuries. The","h":0.016050970589516766},{"c":1,"h":0.019017115455109868,"t":"ancient Greek historian Thucydides, for instance, glorified pirates' daring attacks on ships","x":0.12731007004395528,"y":0.35162241874244105,"w":0.75770019531249999},{"x":0.12731007656572862,"w":0.76180694580078123,"t":"or even cities. For Greeks, piracy was a part of everyday life. Even high-ranking members","y":0.37050147476491979,"h":0.017699115044247704,"c":1},{"y":0.38953488383556922,"t":"of the state were not beyond engaging in such activities. According to the Greek orator","h":0.016069835899150564,"x":0.12731006569312872,"c":1,"w":0.73305953979492189},{"t":"Demosthenes, in 355 BCE, Athenian ambassadors made a detour from their official travel","y":0.40697674420959684,"w":0.75770019531249999,"h":0.017507031533570472,"c":1,"x":0.12731006650226162},{"h":0.01601581235902505,"c":1,"w":0.72279261271158857,"t":"to capture a ship sailing from Egypt, taking the wealth found onboard for themselves!","x":0.12731005906281534,"y":0.42587209313834395},{"h":0.022055254010675873,"y":0.43988044329190745,"x":0.12716124014312583,"t":"The Greeks' liberal approach towards piracy does not mean they always tolerated it,","w":0.71077784220377604,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"but attempts to curtail piracy were hampered by the large number of pirates operating in","w":0.74127309163411459,"x":0.12731006598848221,"y":0.46075581397720788,"h":0.017441860412777732},{"h":0.016881586598084142,"c":1,"w":0.16276041666666669,"x":0.12706175840375444,"y":0.47741589768116932,"t":"the Mediterranean."},{"x":0.12723206311659679,"t":"The rising power of ancient Rome required the Roman Republic to deal with piracy in the","y":0.50536044826112791,"h":0.018611129265619253,"w":0.7578470357259115,"c":1},{"t":"Mediterranean. While piracy was a serious issue for the Republic, Rome profited greatly","h":0.01599866197524169,"c":1,"w":0.74537989298502605,"x":0.12731005339489174,"y":0.52470930244092817},{"y":0.54215116290619481,"w":0.73305953979492189,"h":0.015988371857499684,"t":"from its existence. Pirate raids provided a steady source of slaves, essential for Rome's","c":1,"x":0.12731006572765902},{"x":0.1252566794152791,"w":0.79055440266927079,"h":0.017447863215893755,"c":1,"t":"agriculture and mining industries. But this arrangement could work only while the pirates left","y":0.55958702047523345},{"w":0.78659245808919265,"t":"Roman interests alone. Pirate attacks on grain ships, which were essential to Roman citizens,","h":0.019964907935938636,"c":1,"x":0.12518975930287865,"y":0.57684557690068627},{"h":0.017501886756019269,"w":0.78644765218098955,"t":"led to angry voices in the Senate, demanding punishment of the culprits. Rome, however, did","y":0.59587020623878428,"x":0.12525666661970869,"c":1},{"y":0.61261332532112434,"t":"nothing, further encouraging piracy. By the Ist century BCE, emboldened pirates kidnapped","x":0.12518726917680037,"w":0.78041453043619791,"c":1,"h":0.019572276562715984},{"x":0.12525667121336917,"t":"prominent Roman dignitaries, asking for a large ransom to be paid. Their most famous","y":0.6321533920922644,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"w":0.73100616455078127},{"y":0.64970930234839641,"x":0.12525666520844822,"h":0.017547334541613391,"t":"hostage was none other than Julius Caesar, captured in 75 BCE.","c":1,"w":0.54209447224934892},{"w":0.73100616455078116,"h":0.016027817402617384,"c":1,"y":0.67728613596503207,"x":0.123203283093839,"t":"By now, Rome was well aware that pirates had outlived their usefulness. The time had"},{"w":0.77207392374674477,"c":1,"y":0.69469026570818337,"h":0.017519036577162805,"x":0.12525667230891543,"t":"come for concerted action. In 67 BCE, a new law granted Pompey vast funds to combat the"},{"w":0.78644760131835934,"x":0.12731007862726793,"y":0.7120943953500749,"h":0.017699115044247704,"c":1,"t":"Mediterranean menace. Taking personal command, Pompey divided the entire Mediterranean"},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"x":0.12525667173757266,"t":"into 13 districts, assigning a fleet and commander to each. After cleansing one district of","w":0.74743326822916667,"y":0.73097345157384552},{"c":1,"w":0.73305953979492189,"x":0.12525667739525659,"y":0.74854651173790732,"h":0.01605525790414275,"t":"pirates, the fleet would join another in the next district. The process continued until the"},{"y":0.76598837211658932,"x":0.12525667895624129,"h":0.017492454101202481,"t":"entire Mediterranean was free of pirates. Although thousands of pirates died at the hands of","w":0.77412729899088539,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Pompey's troops, as a long-term solution to the problem, many more were offered land in","y":0.78325530457772874,"w":0.75577209472656248,"h":0.02041155834816899,"x":0.12518831131714875},{"w":0.75385208129882819,"h":0.020879819751840833,"c":1,"t":"fertile areas located far from the sea. Instead of a maritime menace, Rome got productive","y":0.79991777765157657,"x":0.12511928809684017},{"y":0.81737886632245538,"c":1,"t":"farmers that further boosted its economy.","h":0.02002896221689765,"w":0.35163823445638021,"x":0.125009378064035},{"w":0.02669404347737625,"t":"21","y":0.92296511651460966,"h":0.013081394746943587,"c":1,"x":0.88501026769663027},{"y":0.939023246385844,"h":0.047780971470835598,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51825223579186064,"w":0.45180328369140621,"c":1}],"h":3390,"w":2400}